(2) Daily sales receipts and invoices showing liquor, beer, malt beverages and wine separately;
(3) Daily cash register receipts;
(4) Monthly Georgia Sales and Use Tax Reports; and
(5) Federal Income Tax Returns with all Form 1099's.
(Ord. No. 1698, § I, 5-3-2022)

224:
Carrying or consuming an open container of alcoholic beverage in the following areas is prohibited and such areas are not included in the district:
(1) Vehicular travel lanes of roadways;
(2) Vehicular parking spaces and parking lots;
(3) Landscape islands, planter beds or similar landscaping structures;
(4) Any areas that are otherwise restricted, including, but not limited to, utility compounds, stormwater infrastructure and similar property; and
(5) Any and all other areas within the city not expressly permitted herein.
(Ord. No. 2149, § I, 9-2-2025)

225:
Only the following commercial businesses are eligible to sell and dispense open containers of alcoholic beverages in the district:
(1) Those located in building built upon real property located within the district;
